    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678-a3">

                <pb facs="1082" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg946"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    222.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Margron to Mr.
                            Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State of Foreign Relations, Section No.</hi>
                                ——,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 16, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr.<hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    the Government has named Messrs. E. Leon, lawyer; D. Abellard, director of the
                    national foundry; Phocion Da-guerre, chief of the movements of the port of the
                    capital, and P. Jean Jacques, justice of peace of the northern section of this
                    city, members of a commission to proceed conjunctively with those that you will
                    add to take an inventory of the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Haytian
                        Republic.</hi></p>
                <p>I beg you to kindly let me know the names of the members that you will have
                    designated. Please accept, Mr. Minister, the assurance of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>The counselor of the Government charged with the department of foreign
                    relations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eug.
                        Margron.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
